anthra_OSt
==========

anthra is the dark, anthracite skin family for text2skin, designed from 2010
by Tomas Saxer on vdr-portal.de. anthra_OSt is his anthra_1920_OSt (version
20190209) ported to text2skin 2.0; it keeps his design. It is the floating
sibling of anthra_FSt: menu and channel info keep a margin to the edge of the
screen. The original is at http://anthra.de/anthra-skins/.


Requirements
------------

text2skin >= 2.0 (skin format 1.2). An output device with true colour OSD
(e.g. softhddevice, vaapivideo); without it the skin falls back to 256 colours.
The font VDRSymbols Sans by Andreas Mair (Debian: vdrsymbols-ttf).


What is different from anthra_1920_OSt
--------------------------------------

- The skin has a new name, anthra_OSt. Both skins can be installed side by
  side, the options are set anew in the setup menu.
- No build options and no Make.config any more. The skin scales itself to the
  size of the OSD (designed for 1920x1080, tested on 1280x720, 1920x1080 and
  3840x2160); the options are set at runtime in the setup menu of text2skin.
- The menu items are 67 pixels high (DEFAULTHEIGHT), the variant with 61
  pixels is not part of the port.
- EPG images come from a scraper plugin (tvscraper, scraper2vdr) instead of an
  image folder.
- All windows use true colour.


Options
-------

Setup -> Plugins -> text2skin -> "Options of skin 'anthra_OSt'":

  Channel logos                     right    (right, left, none)
  Path of the channel logos         /var/lib/vdr/channellogos
  Main menu logos                   yes
  Menu font                         default  (default, small, large)
  Scrolling text in menus           no
  Timer info in the main menu       yes
  EPG images (scraper)              yes

Channel logos are looked up as <path>/<channel name>.png or
<path>/<channel ID>.png.

The themes (Setup -> OSD -> Theme): darkamber, darkblue, darkorange, default,
izeman, lightamber, lightblue, lightgrey, lightmaroon, white, yabluedefault,
yabluelight.


Installation
------------

  make
  make install

The paths come from vdr.pc if available (skin: <configdir>/plugins/text2skin/
anthra_OSt, themes: <configdir>/themes, translations: <locdir>), otherwise
/var/lib/vdr and /usr/share/locale. DESTDIR is supported.

The skin file anthra_OSt.skin is put together from xml/*.xml.


Translations
------------

The texts of the skin come from Tomas Saxer's translations, Volume and Mute
from the VDR sources. The options are translated into German, Spanish,
Finnish, French, Italian and Dutch, the other languages show them in English.
